# Manual tests (Visual Studio / VS Code REST Client / Rider). Start the API with the "http" profile first:
#   dotnet run --project src/FlixLocadora.Api --launch-profile http
# The CRUD controllers created by CrudGen start [AllowAnonymous]: no token is needed for them yet.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5406

### Health (database included)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Register (default role: Operator)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "dev.user@example.com", "password": "Senha!Forte123" }

### Login → copy data.accessToken
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "dev.user@example.com", "password": "Senha!Forte123" }

### Who am I (Bearer token)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}

### ── Catalog (seed: ./scripts/db-up.ps1 -Seed) ──────────────────────────────

### Movies with a copy to rent right now, by genre
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/movies?genre=Ação&available=true

### Stock of copies (never below the rented ones → 422 MOVIE_COPIES_IN_USE)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/movies/6/copies
Content-Type: application/json

{ "totalCopies": 4 }

### New customer (CPF: 11 digits with valid check digits — 12345678909 is a classic test value)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Gabriela Exemplo", "email": "Gabriela@Example.com", "cpf": "12345678909", "phone": "(11) 98765-0007" }

### ── Rentals ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Rent (the last copy is decided by the database)
# @name rent
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rentals
Content-Type: application/json

{ "movieId": 6, "customerId": 5, "days": 3 }

### Customer 2 has an overdue rental in the seed → 422 CUSTOMER_HAS_OVERDUE_RENTALS
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rentals
Content-Type: application/json

{ "movieId": 6, "customerId": 2, "days": 1 }

### Overdue rentals (status is derived from the dates)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rentals?status=Overdue

### History of a customer
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/customers/1/rentals

### Extend to 5 days from now (UTC; up to Rental:MaxDays after the rental; an overdue rental cannot be extended)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/rentals/{{rent.response.body.$.data.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "dueAt": "{{$datetime iso8601 5 d}}" }

### Return: late fee and total
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rentals/{{rent.response.body.$.data.id}}/return

### Cancel (only within Rental:CancelWindowMinutes of the rental)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/rentals/{{rent.response.body.$.data.id}}
